PYCHARM_DEBUG=1 python backup.py --config /opt/backup/config.yaml
0 3 * * * /usr/bin/python3 /opt/backup/backup.py --config /opt/backup/config.yaml >> /var/log/backup.log 2>&1

Frappe mode (optional)
======================

This is a generic example, not a production target. Never infer the server or
site to deploy to from this README; use only the environment details explicitly
provided for the deployment being configured.

Enable native Frappe backups in the configuration:

    frappe:
      enabled: true
      bench_dir: /home/frappe/frappe-bench
      site: site.example.com

The utility runs this command before passing the result through the existing
local storage, remote upload, rotation, and alert pipeline:

    bench --site site.example.com backup --with-files --compress --backup-path <work-dir>

Run the utility as the operating-system user that owns the Bench. The generic
`paths` and `db` sections are ignored while Frappe mode is enabled.

Production alert standard
=========================

Every TestPro production installation must enable both failure-alert channels:

- Amazon SES SMTP at `email-smtp.us-west-2.amazonaws.com:587` with TLS,
  sending from `info@testpro.io` to `yuriy@testpro.io`.
- Telegram notifications to chat ID `473762021`.

Keep the Amazon SES username/password and Telegram bot token only in the
deployed `config.yaml` with mode `0600`. Never commit real credentials. Send one
test notification through each channel after installation or configuration
changes.

Production installations
========================

After a new project is fully configured and verified, add it to this list as
the final installation step. Record the project/domain, script location, backup
destinations, schedule, retention, and alert channels, but never credentials.
An installation is not complete until this README entry is committed.

- Mautic (`marketing`, `/var/www/mautic`): script in `/opt/mautic-backup`,
  scheduled daily at 03:00 server time. Configured but currently requires
  repair: the job cannot create `/opt/backup/logs` and no local backup directory
  exists at `/var/backups/webapp`.
- Frappe ERP/CRM (`erp.testpro.io`): script in `/opt/backup`, native full-site
  backup with database, site config, public files, and private files. Archives
  are stored locally in `/var/backups/frappe-erp` and uploaded to SharePoint
  `/Frappe/auto`; scheduled daily at 03:00 UTC with seven archives retained.
  Failure alerts are sent through Amazon SES email and Telegram.
- WordPress (`testpro.io`): script in `/home/byi6fra/backup-script`, full
  `public_html` backup (excluding caches and error logs) with a MySQL dump.
  Archives are stored locally in
  `/home/byi6fra/backups/automated-testpro-io` and uploaded to SharePoint
  `/testpro.io`; scheduled daily at 03:00 UTC with seven archives retained.
  Failure alerts are sent through Amazon SES email and Telegram.
